# CODEOWNERS — review gates for the Baileys sidecar supply-chain policy
# (FUL-23 / FUL-24). branch-protection.json sets require_code_owner_reviews:true,
# so an edit to any path below cannot merge without a review from the listed
# owner. That review is the Security sign-off the waiver policy requires.
#
# Placeholder @fullstackforge/* team handles were replaced with the real owner
# (@darshjme) on landing — this is a single-owner repo, so there is no separate
# GitHub team. When a dedicated Security team exists, swap @darshjme for the
# Security team slug on the waiver-register line below.

# Security owns the exception register — adding/renewing a waiver IS a
# Security decision and must not merge without explicit review.
/router/baileys-sidecar/security/osv-waivers.toml   @darshjme

# The gate logic and thresholds themselves are co-owned: DevOps maintains the
# pipeline, Security must approve any change to what the gate enforces.
/router/baileys-sidecar/scripts/osv-gate.mjs        @darshjme
/.github/actions/osv-gate/                          @darshjme
/.github/workflows/baileys-sidecar-*.yml            @darshjme

# Branch-protection config is DevOps-owned infra-as-code.
/ops/                                               @darshjme
